MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_001: Hm, what magic trick should I work on today?\nMaaaybe this one?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_002: Oh! Someone who wants a show? Just a moment!\nAaand, ready!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_003: OK! Sorry to keep you wai...ting?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_004: Mmm.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_005: J-just a moment! {SetColor=Gray}Wh-what's he doing here?!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_006: {SetColor=Gray}The guy attacked Anatolia, and I doubt he's\ninterested in my party tricks... Ahhh, what do I do?!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_007: {SetColor=Gray}Is he gonna kill me?! I've gotta get out of here!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_008: Oh? How swift she is. I will give chase.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_009: Kyah! He's chasing me! Maybe I can hide in here!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_010: She is gone. No, I can sense her, somewhere near...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_011: Please don't find me, please don't find me,\nplease don't find me...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_012: There you are! Hrah!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_013: Aaah!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_014: I have found you. Do you yield?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_015: Hey! You! What are you doing?! Drawing your sword\non that poor, scared girl...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_016: You have no part in this. Tyah!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_017: Waaah!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_018: Nooo! You killed him?! Is this because I ran away?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_019: He is not dead. In fact, he is unscathed. I cut only\nhis armor.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_020: Phew... Even so, you can't just go around slicing\npeople! The gods won't forgive you!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_021: What say do the gods have in it?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_022: I know you're participating in the Heroic Games, but\nthere are limits, you know. Come on, what'd you do?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_023: Uh huh, I figured. Well, I'm really busy, so please\nmind yourself, OK?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_024: Dietrich, that was just plain mean! You made me do\nall the talking!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_025: Ms. Anna kept staring at me with a blank face...\nI got so nervous, I could hardly speak!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_026: When words failed, you conveyed a great deal with\nmere gestures. It was captivating.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_027: One moment... Oh, perhaps not now, but\nlater, certainly.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_028: Phew, he's gone. I don't know what all that was, but\nI guess he's leaving me alone, so that's good.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_C_029: Wait... Wait. He said "later." That means...he's gonna\ncome back?! Noooooo!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_001: So you are here. I have been searching.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_002: Agh, it's you! {SetColor=Gray}Can't. Run. Gotta. Stay. Put! Otherwise\nsomeone might get hurt...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_003: What is considered a typical amount? I am prepared\nto pay.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_004: Huh? Wait, what's the gold for?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_005: Your fee. I was highly entertained.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_006: Um, do you mean when you chased after me and\nslashed at that soldier?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_007: Indeed. The day you went wild in front of Anna. At\nthat time, I lacked funds.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_008: Went...wild? You were the one who acted wild!\nWait, so you came to watch me perform?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_009: No way... If I'd known, I wouldn't have run from you.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_010: I only ran because I was terrified. I can't accept\nyour money.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_011: What? Why not? I was truly entertained.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_012: Moreover...if you feared me then, and so fled, why do\nyou not flee now?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_013: Well, because... When you knocked that soldier\ndown, it reminded me of something...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_014: It made me think about the day someone very special\nto me died. Right in front of me...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_015: I feel like...if running away allows something like that\nto happen, then I have to stand my ground.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_016: Hm. Was the soldier important to you?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_017: No, I didn't know him. But I hate seeing anyone\nget hurt.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_018: I mean, there are times when you've gotta fight. But\nI really don't want to take anyone's life...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_019: So you care for the lives of strangers. I cannot say\nthe same.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_B_020: Hey, you forgot your gold! And he's gone... Did he...\ndid he look kinda jealous or something?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_001: Aaand, presto! The dagger turned into money!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_002: How you waved your right hand to disguise what\nyou were doing with your left... Dexterous!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_003: Heeey, are you teasing me or something? The next\none will be better—just you wait.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_004: Holding two strings and pretending they are one,\nwhile feigning to cut them with a dull blade...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_005: You have a knack for this. I am pleased to witness\nyour technique.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_006: Gah, you saw through every one of my tricks... And I\nspent so much time practicing them!
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_007: Hmm.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_008: What? Just so you know, my frustration? It's not a\nmagic trick.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_009: I was reflecting on the fact that you no longer\nfear me.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_010: Hehe... Oh, I see. I mean, I do think you're right.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_011: At first I was super scared and wondering if you\nwere going to kill me or something.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_012: You and I are worlds apart, so I never know what\nyou're thinking...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_013: But then I started to wonder if maybe we aren't so\ndifferent in some ways.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_014: Hm.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_015: When you came to pay me for the "show," you\nseemed, I dunno...kinda jealous?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_016: Your eyes looked even a little sad, like you were\nseeing something you couldn't ever reach...
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_017: So I decided then and there that I wanted you to\nknow me. And I wanted to know you.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_018: And that maybe we could be friends.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_019: I see. Perhaps we will.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_020: Yeah! Sooo, which trick did you like the most?
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_021: Your wild gesticulations as you groveled to Anna.\nI could not tear my eyes away.
MID_SE_Dit_Hal_A_022: Hey, I told you that wasn't one of my tricks!